      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Following up on the discussion from the previous patchset regarding the `ra` register on RISC-V: since `ra` serves as the Link Register and shouldn\u0027t be stripped, this test will fail on RISC-V if it expects `ra` (which is in `expected_regs` at index 29) to be `0` when `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_PANIC_STRIP_GPR` is enabled.\n\nConsider updating this logic to leave `expected` unchanged for `ra` on RISC-V. This will usefully verify that `ra` is *not* stripped while the other GPRs are:\n\n```c\n\t\tif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_PANIC_STRIP_GPR)) {\n#if defined(CONFIG_RISCV)\n\t\t\t/* The return address (ra) is a code pointer and is intentionally not stripped. */\n\t\t\tif (expected_regs[i].index !\u003d 29 /* ra */)\n#endif\n\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\texpected \u003d 0;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n```",
